WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:08.300
Welcome. Microsoft Copilot is evolving from a
place where you ask for answers into a place

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:13.320
where you can ask, delegate, build, and
automate work. That matters whether you're an individual

3
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.380
contributor, a team leader, an IT professional,
or someone running a smaller business, because

4
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.500
the way you define work for AI increasingly
shapes the value you get from it.

5
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.780
In this session, you'll learn four practical
skills. You'll distinguish between chat, cowork,

6
00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:32.020
code, and autopilot. You'll learn how to define
an assignment instead of giving AI a vague

7
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.940
request. You'll learn how to verify important
outputs against the evidence. And you'll identify

8
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:42.140
recurring processes that can be delegated or
even redesigned rather than simply accelerated.

9
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:46.420
Microsoft describes home as the starting point
where chat and cowork come together, while

10
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:50.900
code lets people build solutions and autopilot
acts as a persistent agent that keeps working

11
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.620
when you're not. Those capabilities support
different kinds of work. So the first skill

12
00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.020
is knowing what kind of work you're actually
handing over.
